# Lessons from the lineup editor rework, 2026-09-24. Read before any UI work.
# Format: TOON (Token-Oriented Object Notation). Tables are name[count]{fields}: then one row per line.

purpose: Product and UX rules the team lead had to point out. Apply them without being told.

working:
  askFirst: "Ask about ambiguous product rules before building. A few quick questions beat a round of corrections."
  thinkAhead: "Before shipping a screen, walk it as each role (member, admin, media) on a phone and on desktop, in view and edit mode."
  componentForward: "Build components with one job, reused rather than copied. One docked bar (SecondNav), one picker, one lineup view that also edits."
  realData: "Preview with real data (scripts/roster.tsv, the live calendar), never invented people or answers."

components[6]{name,job}:
  Lineup.svelte,"Shows the week's lineup; for admins the same rows turn into dropdowns. Save rules come from missingParts (src/lib/lineup.ts)."
  SecondNav.svelte,"The bar docked above BottomNav on phones. Holds one thing at a time."
  RsvpCard.svelte,"Your answer plus everyone's responses. Docks its buttons in SecondNav when you're assigned."
  BottomNav.svelte,"App navigation. SecondNav assumes its 53px height."
  admin/People.svelte,"The team for superadmins: ministry and access filters, A–Z sort; a table on PC (900px and up), cards on phones. Edits in place."
  admin/UserForm.svelte,"Add or edit one person. Two columns with `wide` for the table row. Primary role only offers what they play.""

rules[19]{area,rule}:
  editing,"Edit in place: dropdowns replace the names in the same rows. Never open a separate form."
  picker,"List only people marked for the slot's part, under a heading naming it. No 'Everyone else' group. 'Someone else…' lets you type a name."
  picker,"One person, one spot per week. Anyone already placed is hidden from other dropdowns on the same side (band or media)."
  picker,"Picking someone from the other side moves them (Chan: Media to Bass). No 'moves from' note."
  save,"Save needs a Praise Leader, one more vocalist in any other vocal slot, Drums, a guitarist (L. or R. Guitar) and Media. One rule, missingParts in src/lib/lineup.ts: the editor keeps Save off and the server rejects the rest."
  parts,"New parts pick an emoji separately from the name, so every label starts with one. Keys is an optional preset, not a standard slot."
  media,"Media is dropdown rows plus '+ Add media team'. No chips, no free-text box."
  rsvp,"Show each assigned person's answer next to their name: ✅ yes, 🤔 maybe, ❌ no, grey dash for no answer."
  rsvp,"No RSVP anywhere in edit mode. Editing is about who's assigned, not who's coming."
  rsvp,"Only people on a week's lineup can answer for it. Everyone else sees the responses, nothing more."
  secondnav,"Dock your RSVP only on weeks you're on the lineup. While editing, SecondNav holds Cancel and Save instead."
  people,"Mobile first, but PC gets power: a real table with sortable headers, not stretched cards."
  people,"Filter by ministry part (Vocals, Drums, Guitar, Bass, Keys, Media) and by access (Member, Admin, Superadmin). Filters survive switching widths."
  people,"Primary role is its own field (UserRecord.primaryRole), not guessed from the first listed part. It must be one of the things they do."
  preview,"Every screen worth changing gets a /dev/preview page on real roster data, so it can be checked without signing in."
  style,"DM Sans. Deliberate, calm layout; nothing that looks templated."
  data,"The part matrix is scripts/roster.tsv (gitignored, has emails). It must never reach a build or a commit."
  data,"SLOT_PARTS in src/lib/parts.ts (which parts fill which slot) is an assumption, not from the roster. Confirm before relying on it."
  week,"The week's theme is the service event's title; the Motif line is a colour. Theme and YouTube playlist are edited in the same edit mode, in the WeekDetails spot (src/lib/week-info.ts)."

answered[4]{question,answer}:
  "Does 'backup' in the save rule mean the Second Praise Leader slot?","No: any second vocalist, in any vocal slot"
  "Should people not on a week's lineup be able to RSVP for it?","No: they only see the responses"
  "Should the server reject incomplete lineups too?","Yes: the lineup endpoint checks missingParts"
  "Is the Theme the event title or the Motif line?","The event title. A placeholder title (\"Week's Theme\") counts as no theme"

openQuestions[1]{question,currentAnswer}:
  "Should the RSVP endpoint also refuse answers from people not on the lineup?","Not yet: only the app hides the buttons"
